{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837968",
      "title": "Getting Values via FormData & Native Browser APIs",
      "sourceHash": "8533ae14bd0316b94a6df3020c21624e0e0908c02f9fd975736f008cdf1be237",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 3.36,
          "en": "So let's explore another solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.36,
          "end": 6.09,
          "en": "for extracting user input values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.09,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "which can be a bit more convenient to work with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "when dealing with more complex forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 16.26,
          "en": "So now to explore a more complex form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.26,
          "end": 19.23,
          "en": "and how we can handle the submission of such a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 23.1,
          "en": "and the extraction of values from such a form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.1,
          "end": 27.69,
          "en": "attached to this lecture, you'll find a Signup.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.69,
          "end": 31.173,
          "en": "which you can simply add to your components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.46,
          "end": 36.63,
          "en": "and in the App component you can and should now import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.63,
          "end": 41.63,
          "en": "this Signup component from components Signup.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.09,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "and you can replace this Login component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 47.38,
          "en": "with that Signup component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.02,
          "end": 52.56,
          "en": "and you can get rid of the Login import therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 54.51,
          "en": "and with that you should see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 57.363,
          "en": "this more complex form on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 62.7,
          "en": "Now handling the submission of such a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.7,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "works in the same way as it did for a simpler form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 69.94,
          "en": "You can add a handleSubmit function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 75.093,
          "en": "and connect this to the onSubmit prop like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 76.02,
          "end": 78.57,
          "en": "And then here you'll get this event object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.57,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "and you want to call event.preventDefault to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 84.592,
          "en": "that this automatically generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84.592,
          "end": 87.60300000000001,
          "en": "HTTP request is not being sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.03999999999999,
          "end": 92.78999999999999,
          "en": "But it's now the extraction of all those entered values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.78999999999999,
          "end": 97.62,
          "en": "in all those input fields that can be a bit tricky,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 102.09,
          "en": "because you can of course use state and revs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 102.09,
          "end": 106.62,
          "en": "but setting up and handling all those different state values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 106.62,
          "end": 111.50999999999999,
          "en": "or all those different revs can of course be a lot of work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 115.08,
          "en": "And that's why you should also at least consider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 115.08,
          "end": 118.77000000000001,
          "en": "using a native built-in feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 121.69,
          "en": "for getting hold of all those values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 122.76,
          "end": 127.17,
          "en": "because it turns out that the browser actually helps you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 127.17,
          "end": 129.3,
          "en": "with handling that form submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 129.3,
          "end": 132.093,
          "en": "and getting hold of all the entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 133.17,
          "end": 135.33,
          "en": "It helps you by allowing you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 135.33,
          "end": 137.904,
          "en": "to create a special kind of object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 137.904,
          "end": 141.57,
          "en": "based on a special kind of constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 141.57,
          "end": 144,
          "en": "that's built into the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 144,
          "end": 146.943,
          "en": "the FormData constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 148.59,
          "end": 153.24,
          "en": "This is built into the browser, not provided by me or React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 153.24,
          "end": 158.07,
          "en": "and FormData is an object that makes it easy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 158.07,
          "end": 162.243,
          "en": "to get hold of the different values entered into a form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 166.38,
          "en": "For that you just need to pass that form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 166.38,
          "end": 169.98,
          "en": "as an input to FormData, and you can do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 169.98,
          "end": 173.97,
          "en": "by simply passing event.target to FormData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 173.97,
          "end": 178.56,
          "en": "because the target of this submit event is that form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 178.56,
          "end": 181.743,
          "en": "because it is that form that was submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 183.48,
          "end": 187.74,
          "en": "So therefore as a result you'll get back a FormData object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 187.74,
          "end": 190.2,
          "en": "that will in the end give you access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 190.2,
          "end": 194.343,
          "en": "to the data that was added to all the inputs in that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 195.6,
          "end": 198.45,
          "en": "Now for this to work all those inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 198.45,
          "end": 200.85,
          "en": "for which you wanna extract values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 200.85,
          "end": 204.423,
          "en": "must have that name prop set on them though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 209.67000000000002,
          "en": "So all your input fields, even if they're not input fields,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 209.67000000000002,
          "end": 211.95,
          "en": "but select fields for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 211.95,
          "end": 216.303,
          "en": "must have that name attribute, that name prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 217.5,
          "end": 220.89,
          "en": "You'll find that on all the input fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 220.89,
          "end": 223.82999999999998,
          "en": "and you need that for FormData to work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 223.82999999999998,
          "end": 227.61,
          "en": "and to give you access to the entered values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 227.61,
          "end": 230.79,
          "en": "because now you can use this FormData object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 230.79,
          "end": 233.55,
          "en": "to call one of the built-in methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 233.55,
          "end": 235.39,
          "en": "for example the get method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 236.28,
          "end": 239.523,
          "en": "to extract the value for a specific name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 240.45,
          "end": 243.3,
          "en": "So for example, here I could get the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 243.3,
          "end": 247.47,
          "en": "for the input field that has the name email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 247.47,
          "end": 250.623,
          "en": "which would be this input field here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 252.87,
          "end": 255.99,
          "en": "So calling get on this form data object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 255.99,
          "end": 259.77,
          "en": "would give me the entered email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 259.77,
          "end": 261.963,
          "en": "and I could then extract and use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 263.28,
          "end": 266.91,
          "en": "Now we could repeat that for all the input fields,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 266.91,
          "end": 268.98,
          "en": "so for example also for the password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 268.98,
          "end": 271.53,
          "en": "to get the entered password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 271.53,
          "end": 273.99,
          "en": "but we therefore of course would end up with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 273.99,
          "end": 276.9,
          "en": "quite a lot of code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 276.9,
          "end": 281.85,
          "en": "Therefore, a common pattern or trick that's often used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 281.85,
          "end": 285.9,
          "en": "to quickly get hold of all the entered values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 285.9,
          "end": 288.81,
          "en": "and group them together into an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 288.81,
          "end": 292.8,
          "en": "is to use the built-in Object class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 292.8,
          "end": 295.86,
          "en": "which is also provided by the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 295.86,
          "end": 300.86,
          "en": "and call the fromEntries static method on that class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 301.14,
          "end": 304.77,
          "en": "and pass the FormData object to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 304.77,
          "end": 309.48,
          "en": "To be precise, pass the result of calling the entries method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 309.48,
          "end": 313.573,
          "en": "on that FormData object to object fromEntries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 314.7,
          "end": 318.42,
          "en": "This might look a bit weird, but in the end, calling entries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 318.42,
          "end": 322.62,
          "en": "on the FormData object will give us kind of an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 322.62,
          "end": 326.83,
          "en": "of all the input fields and their values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 327.81,
          "end": 331.5,
          "en": "and calling Object from entries on that array then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 331.5,
          "end": 336.5,
          "en": "will simply give us an object where we have key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 338.883,
          "en": "for all our input fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 340.26,
          "end": 343.24,
          "en": "So if I console log data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 344.13,
          "end": 348.15,
          "en": "and I submit this form by clicking Sign up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 348.15,
          "end": 350.22,
          "en": "you'll see I get an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 350.22,
          "end": 353.67,
          "en": "where I have different key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 353.67,
          "end": 356.493,
          "en": "one for every input I have in this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 357.45,
          "end": 362.45,
          "en": "So for my first name, last name, email, password and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 363.09,
          "end": 366.12,
          "en": "Though once taking a closer look here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 366.12,
          "end": 369.3,
          "en": "you might notice that one input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 369.3,
          "end": 372.36,
          "en": "is missing here in this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 372.36,
          "end": 376.53,
          "en": "and that would be this How did you find us input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 376.53,
          "end": 379.803,
          "en": "which is actually a group of inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 381,
          "end": 386,
          "en": "This how did you find us area in the end is a group",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 386.13,
          "end": 390.79,
          "en": "of check boxes, which all have the same name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 392.04,
          "end": 394.68,
          "en": "because in the end here I want to get an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 394.68,
          "end": 397.53,
          "en": "of all the checked values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 397.53,
          "end": 400.14,
          "en": "so all the values of the boxes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 400.14,
          "end": 402.93,
          "en": "that have been checked by the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 402.93,
          "end": 407.7,
          "en": "and such multi value input fields are lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 407.7,
          "end": 410.823,
          "en": "when using entries and fromEntries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 411.9,
          "end": 415.17,
          "en": "But you can thankfully easily get them back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 415.17,
          "end": 418.8,
          "en": "by manually extracting and storing them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 418.8,
          "end": 421.893,
          "en": "So here I can get my acquisitionChannel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 425.64,
          "end": 427.847,
          "en": "by using FormData getAll,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 428.94,
          "end": 430.68,
          "en": "which is the method you want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 430.68,
          "end": 434.493,
          "en": "if you want to get multiple values from one input field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 435.33,
          "end": 439.02,
          "en": "which you, for example need if you have multiple check boxes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 439.02,
          "end": 441.15,
          "en": "that all have the same name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 441.15,
          "end": 445.86,
          "en": "and you want to get the values of all check boxes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 445.86,
          "end": 448.02,
          "en": "then you can use getAll",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 448.02,
          "end": 451.56,
          "en": "with the name that's set up on the checkbox elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 451.56,
          "end": 453.483,
          "en": "so in this case acquisition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 454.56,
          "end": 458.76,
          "en": "and you pass that to getAll and that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 458.76,
          "end": 461.22,
          "en": "Now we also have the acquisition channel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 461.22,
          "end": 464.13,
          "en": "and we could merge it into this data object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 464.13,
          "end": 466.239,
          "en": "by adding a new property to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 466.239,
          "end": 468.9,
          "en": "which could be called acquisition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 468.9,
          "end": 471.627,
          "en": "and which is equal to acquisitionChannel,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 472.92,
          "end": 475.32,
          "en": "which will be an array of all the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 475.32,
          "end": 477.813,
          "en": "selected by this acquisition input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 479.22,
          "end": 482.7,
          "en": "And therefore, now if I console log data thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 482.7,
          "end": 484.86,
          "en": "after adding the acquisition property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 484.86,
          "end": 489.72,
          "en": "with all those selected values and we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 489.72,
          "end": 494.04,
          "en": "if I reload this and maybe select two values here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 494.04,
          "end": 496.5,
          "en": "if I click Sign up, you'll see that now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
